@ConsciousExpression For someone working in that industry for almost 20 years you are shockingly bad informed and lack reading comprehension.

The client of a stock broker is the one paying them. That can be the one looking to purchase stock or the one trying to sell their stock. In this case the company trying to sell shares were the clients and the fiduciary duty is solely towards that company.

That said you are correct. Lying about a stock to increase its value is fraud and always illegal. That said I also never said that what happens in this clip is actually legal now did I?

