@wba1987 From my perspective as a Muslim, I would say that we should seek protection and sustenance from Allah, and ask Him to protect us from unexpected losses whether it’s a broken fridge, car repairs, medical bills, or other hardships.

At the same time, we should earn our money through halal means and avoid things forbidden in Islam, such as gambling. You may think you’ve gained money through something like the lottery, but without barakah, that wealth may not bring lasting benefit or peace.

When we put our trust in Allah, we understand that sustenance is not just about having more money, but about having barakah and contentment in what we have. Otherwise, no matter how much a person earns, they may constantly feel that it is never enough and live in fear and stress over losing it.

