@PimpRat  Confidence isn't just about how you act or speak, it's an internal emotional state.

If an actor plays a brave soldier on screen perfectly, we don't say the actor is actually brave. They are just good at acting brave. A con artist is just an actor whose stage is real life. 

They aren't actually experiencing the emotion of being confident, unless they beleive their own lie, which to be fair is entirely possible.
